l,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.4.stable.official [4c311cbee] but has been happening for as long as I can remember (4.3, 4.2)\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.stable - macOS Sequoia (15.1.0) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M1 Max (Apple7) - Apple M1 Max (10 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen dragging a bezier point texture looks different from what it does the moment you release it. Note that this only happen when the point tangents aren't parallel to the x axis. Seems like tangents get lost and an unrotated point gets submitted on drag\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bd12700f-fb8e-473a-a224-2ae8c59e216f\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open the material on the plane in MRP and find the CurveTexture in albedo\n2. Create a new point and tweak it's tangent to make it a random angle\n3. Pay attention to what happens when you stop dragging the point and _release_ the left mouse button\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[curve_mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19145488/curve_mrp.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"passivestar","id":60579014,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTc5MDE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60579014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar","html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/subscriptions","organizati